<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Rain seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Rain seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast scattered showers in the Western, Central and Sabaragamuwa provinces and in the Galle, Matara and Kurunegala districts for Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Tuesday that thundershowers may develop in the Uva and Eastern provinces during Wednesday afternoon or evening.</p>
<p>The department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Tuesday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   69.0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	   102.7</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  15.1</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 89.7</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     52.5</p>
<p>    Norton		  115.0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0.7</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0.5</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   1.8</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  1.1</p>
</text>
